## Measure early, on the target

Trusted evaluation is the only source of a number that counts, and it runs where the
objective is measured, on the target hardware and in the target environment. Unless the
environment notes say this editor has that hardware attached, its devices, libraries and
paths say nothing about the target, so a missing accelerator or package here is no reason to
skip measuring. When they do, use it to reproduce a failed evaluation's case before you
resubmit; the editor checks that the code runs, the trusted evaluation checks that it is
correct and fast.

Do not spend a whole turn on one large change. Make the smallest change that builds and
passes the cheapest local check, submit it with `submit_evaluation`, and only then extend it,
submitting again after each further step that works. A turn that ends with a large change
that was never submitted leaves the reviewer and the planner nothing to judge it by.
